WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.657
The four button drone is back

2
00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:07.403
with buttons u, v

3
00:00:07.403 --> 00:00:10.068
w and s as the columns of A.

4
00:00:10.068 --> 00:00:13.652
A delivery is due at two, five, three.

5
00:00:13.652 --> 00:00:17.420
Another customer asks for one, one, one.

6
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.803
One recipe for the delivery

7
00:00:20.803 --> 00:00:22.644
one u and one v.

8
00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:25.568
East: one plus one is two.

9
00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:28.926
North: two plus three is five.

10
00:00:28.926 --> 00:00:31.850
Up: one plus two is three.

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.247
Another recipe: two v and minus one s.

12
00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:39.549
Two minus zero, six minus one

13
00:00:39.549 --> 00:00:43.809
four minus one: two, five, three again.

14
00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.152
We want every recipe

15
00:00:46.152 --> 00:00:49.880
and a test for the other customer.

16
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.982
Eliminate on A with b attached

17
00:00:52.982 --> 00:00:54.284
carrying b one

18
00:00:54.284 --> 00:00:56.725
b two and b three as letters.

19
00:00:56.725 --> 00:00:59.980
The steps are the same three as before.

20
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.687
After two steps

21
00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:05.418
rows two and three are zero, one, one, one

22
00:01:05.503 --> 00:01:08.217
with b two minus two b one and b

23
00:01:08.302 --> 00:01:10.931
three minus b one on the right.

24
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:13.984
Then row three minus row two leaves

25
00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:15.934
all zeros on the left

26
00:01:16.019 --> 00:01:18.224
and b one minus b two plus

27
00:01:18.309 --> 00:01:20.090
b three on the right.

28
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.189
That row says zero equals b one

29
00:01:23.278 --> 00:01:25.494
minus b two plus b three.

30
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.509
So the system is solvable exactly

31
00:01:28.598 --> 00:01:30.815
when that number is zero

32
00:01:30.904 --> 00:01:33.209
the target must lie in the

33
00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:35.160
plane of lecture six.

34
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.614
Test the delivery

35
00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:41.259
two minus five plus three is zero.

36
00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:42.300
Solvable.

37
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.164
Test one, one, one

38
00:01:45.164 --> 00:01:49.265
one minus one plus one is one.

39
00:01:49.265 --> 00:01:54.028
The last row reads zero equals one

40
00:01:54.028 --> 00:01:56.410
no recipe at all.

41
00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.950
The new button s also passes

42
00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.580
zero minus one plus one is zero.

43
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.440
So s reaches nothing new.

44
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:11.176
Without eliminating again: is three, four

45
00:02:11.176 --> 00:02:12.742
one reachable?

46
00:02:12.742 --> 00:02:15.039
And zero, zero, five?

47
00:02:15.039 --> 00:02:16.710
Pause and test.

48
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.340
Three minus four plus one is zero: yes.

49
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.420
Zero minus zero plus five is five: no.

50
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.127
Here is the same test in

51
00:02:33.215 --> 00:02:35.165
a picture we can draw.

52
00:02:35.165 --> 00:02:39.153
Take the two by two matrix with columns one

53
00:02:39.153 --> 00:02:40.925
two and three, six.

54
00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:43.495
Both columns lie on one line

55
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:45.267
through the origin

56
00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:48.280
so the column space is that line.

57
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.888
The target four, eight is on the line

58
00:02:51.974 --> 00:02:54.032
elimination leaves eight

59
00:02:54.118 --> 00:02:56.433
minus two times four, zero.

60
00:02:56.433 --> 00:02:57.290
Solvable.

61
00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.634
The target four, nine is off the line

62
00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.778
nine minus eight is one

63
00:03:02.778 --> 00:03:05.950
and zero equals one has no solution.

64
00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.508
Back to the drone.

65
00:03:08.508 --> 00:03:13.452
For a solvable target, the reduced rows say

66
00:03:13.452 --> 00:03:18.286
x one plus two x three minus x four is one

67
00:03:18.286 --> 00:03:23.010
and x two plus x three plus x four is one.

68
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.049
For a particular solution

69
00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:29.359
set the free variables to zero.

70
00:03:29.359 --> 00:03:33.082
Then x one is one and x two is one

71
00:03:33.082 --> 00:03:36.082
x p is one, one, zero, zero

72
00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.840
one u and one v.

73
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.119
In the small example

74
00:03:40.211 --> 00:03:42.968
the one equation left is x one

75
00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.724
plus three x two equals four.

76
00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:49.491
Set the free x two to zero: x p is four

77
00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:53.350
zero, drawn here in the plane of amounts.

78
00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.725
Now add the nullspace.

79
00:03:55.807 --> 00:03:58.907
For the small matrix it is this orange

80
00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:01.436
line through minus three, one.

81
00:04:01.436 --> 00:04:03.476
Keep it as a faint copy

82
00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.598
and slide it over to x p

83
00:04:05.679 --> 00:04:08.209
every point of the shifted gold

84
00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.330
line solves the equation.

85
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.190
Why?

86
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:16.288
A times x minus x p is b minus b, zero

87
00:04:16.415 --> 00:04:19.601
so any solution minus x p

88
00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:22.533
lies in the nullspace

89
00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.356
and adding a nullspace vector

90
00:04:26.484 --> 00:04:29.160
keeps A x equal to b.

91
00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.083
For the drone

92
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:35.129
x is x p plus c s one plus d s two.

93
00:04:35.129 --> 00:04:39.961
c equal to one gives minus one, zero, one

94
00:04:39.961 --> 00:04:40.636
zero.

95
00:04:40.636 --> 00:04:44.457
Check: minus one plus three, two

96
00:04:44.457 --> 00:04:47.603
minus two plus seven, five

97
00:04:47.603 --> 00:04:50.750
minus one plus four, three.

98
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.790
c equal to zero and d equal

99
00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:57.377
to minus one gives zero, two, zero

100
00:04:57.377 --> 00:05:01.860
minus one: the second recipe from the start.

101
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.010
Infinitely many solutions does

102
00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:07.152
not mean anything works.

103
00:05:07.152 --> 00:05:10.237
Try one, zero in the small example

104
00:05:10.237 --> 00:05:12.978
one plus zero is one, not four.

105
00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:15.720
The point is off the gold line.

106
00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.783
For the drone, one, zero, zero

107
00:05:18.783 --> 00:05:21.320
zero lands at one, two, one

108
00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.158
not at the delivery.

109
00:05:23.158 --> 00:05:26.220
Only x p plus the nullspace works

110
00:05:26.308 --> 00:05:29.283
and a single answer from a library

111
00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.470
is only one point of it.

112
00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:36.015
So: eliminate on A with b attached.

113
00:05:36.015 --> 00:05:40.320
Each zero row gives a condition on b

114
00:05:40.433 --> 00:05:44.058
and zero equals a nonzero number

115
00:05:44.171 --> 00:05:46.210
means no solution.

116
00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.526
When b passes, the complete solution is

117
00:05:50.627 --> 00:05:54.491
x p plus the nullspace: the null line

118
00:05:54.491 --> 00:05:57.440
shifted to pass through x p.

119
00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:01.638
Your turn: can the drone reach four, nine

120
00:06:01.638 --> 00:06:02.187
five?

121
00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:03.378
In part two

122
00:06:03.378 --> 00:06:07.501
the rank tells how many solutions there are

123
00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.150
before you solve.
